<header class="resume-heading"><h1>Conor Brown</h1><p><strong>Software Engineer · C#/.NET · Payments &amp; Distributed Systems</strong></p><p>Oklahoma, USA · <a href="mailto:carllbrown87@gmail.com">carllbrown87@gmail.com</a> · <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/conor--brown/">LinkedIn</a> · <a href="https://github.com/conorbrown-dev">GitHub</a></p></header>
<section><h2>Professional summary</h2><p>Software engineer with 12+ years of professional .NET experience, including four years building payment services and billing telemetry at IXOPAY. Designs and delivers event-driven backend systems on Azure using domain-driven design and CQRS, and owns work from architecture through production. Supports a team of 10 developers through architecture reviews, design workshops, and mentoring. Uses AI-assisted development daily across implementation, testing, and debugging, with clear standards for validating generated code.</p></section>
<section><h2>Selected impact</h2><ul>
<li><strong>Built a containerized Card Account Updater service</strong> to reduce subscription churn caused by expiring payment credentials.</li>
<li>Engineered asynchronous API usage telemetry on Azure Service Bus, designed around a <strong>99.9% delivery SLA</strong> for billing data used across the company and by enterprise customers.</li>
<li><strong>Led the migration from on-premises hosting to Azure,</strong> modernizing a legacy .NET Framework MVC application to .NET 10 and merging the legacy codebase into the modern application. The work covered Azure App Service, runtime configuration, Entra integration, Key Vault identity, parallel pipelines, staging validation, and rollback planning.</li>
<li>Reduced deployment time from <strong>45 minutes to 10 minutes</strong> as a result of the Azure migration.</li>
<li><strong>Introduced domain-driven design practices:</strong> led event-storming and DDD sessions to make business rules and ownership explicit, then implemented the resulting DDD/CQRS workflow and rule-builder capabilities across aggregates, APIs, persistence, UI, and end-to-end tests.</li>
<li><strong>Replaced Elasticsearch with SQL and in-memory caching,</strong> removing a dependency that caused deployment and local development issues and could not be reached from Azure without a paid cloud instance.</li>
<li><strong>Built Mega Desk, an agent harness used daily by teammates,</strong> integrating Claude Agent SDK and Codex CLI with Azure DevOps work-item prioritization, PR reviews, comment resolution, and merge-conflict workflows, with human diff review before delivery actions.</li>
</ul></section>
