<li>Led the migration from on-premises hosting to Azure App Service, merging the legacy codebase into the modern application; covered runtime configuration, Entra integration, Key Vault identity, parallel pipelines, staging validation, and rollback planning.</li>
<li>Reduced deployment time from 45 minutes to 10 minutes as a result of the Azure migration.</li>
<li>Implemented DDD/CQRS workflow and rule-builder capabilities across aggregates, APIs, persistence, UI, and end-to-end testing.</li>
<li>Guides a team of 10 developers through design decisions, architecture reviews, and code reviews; led event-storming and DDD implementation sessions to make business rules and ownership explicit.</li>
<li>Moved end-to-end testing into the application repository with Playwright-based regression coverage; reduced core test execution from 8–9 minutes to approximately 21 seconds through coverage-tooling changes.</li>
<li>Replaced Elasticsearch with SQL queries and in-memory caching, removing a dependency that caused deployment and local development issues.</li>
<li>Uses Claude Code in implementation, refactoring, testing, and legacy-code workflows; checks proposed changes against domain rules, architecture boundaries, tests, and review before delivery. Codified engineering standards in a CLAUDE.md reference guide covering DDD, dependency boundaries, modern C#, and a reference vertical slice.</li>
</ul>
